# Channel check: does each bus reach its own outputs?
# (specs/miniaudio-devices/spec.md requirement 18, and its manual criterion
# "Channel order on the Inpulse 500".)
#
# Deck 1 plays 440 Hz on the main bus only, outputs 1 and 2: the speakers.
# Deck 2 plays 880 Hz on the headphone bus only, outputs 3 and 4: its fader
# is down, its PFL is on, and the cue mix is all cue. For 30 seconds:
#
#     ks-harness --channels 4 src/apps/harness/scripts/channels.harness
#
# Right: the speakers play only the low tone, and the headphones play only
# the high tone, in both ears.
# Wrong: the high tone also comes out of the speakers, or only one ear of the
# headphones has it.
#
# On PipeWire, while it plays, `pw-dump` shows the ks-harness stream's format.
# Its channel positions should be the sink's (FL FR RL RR on the Inpulse).

track low sine 440 30
track high sine 880 30

0 main -12
0 headphones -12
0 cuemix 0
0 load 1 low
0 play 1
0 load 2 high
0 fader 2 0
0 pfl 2 on
0 play 2

30 end
